From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BukkitPatcher <bukkitpatcher@local.dev>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 14:08:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Skip BlockPhysicsEvent if no listeners

BlockPhysicsEvent creates a new CraftBlock instance and clones
CraftBlockData on construction, which is expensive with many
neighbor updates and often has no plugin listening. Reuse the
existing ServerLevel#hasPhysicsEvent flag (already maintained
elsewhere in this codebase) to skip event construction entirely
when there are no listeners.

Backported from Leaf ver/26.2 (original author: Dreeam) to ver/1.21.4.
NeighborUpdater.java in 1.21.4 has an additional cworld != null guard
not present upstream; the hasPhysicsEvent check is added alongside it.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/redstone/NeighborUpdater.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/redstone/NeighborUpdater.java
index 26c15c60d358273a3b369c286771c81d6f0979dd..4bae5c458259025eb9b8b45c5aa5fc13aab44476 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/redstone/NeighborUpdater.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/redstone/NeighborUpdater.java
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ public interface NeighborUpdater {
         try {
             // CraftBukkit start
             org.bukkit.craftbukkit.CraftWorld cworld = level.getWorld();
-            if (cworld != null) {
+            if (cworld != null && level instanceof net.minecraft.server.level.ServerLevel serverLevel && serverLevel.hasPhysicsEvent) { // Leaf - Skip BlockPhysicsEvent if no listeners
                 org.bukkit.event.block.BlockPhysicsEvent event = new org.bukkit.event.block.BlockPhysicsEvent(org.bukkit.craftbukkit.block.CraftBlock.at(level, pos), org.bukkit.craftbukkit.block.data.CraftBlockData.fromData(state), org.bukkit.craftbukkit.block.CraftBlock.at(level, sourcePos)); // Paper - Add source block to BlockPhysicsEvent
                 level.getCraftServer().getPluginManager().callEvent(event);
 
